      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Installation and Configuration Guide**\n\n**General Specifications**\n\nThe Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor operates within a voltage range of 3.3V to 5.0V DC and utilizes a 4-pin header for connection. Interface with other components is achieved via the I2C protocol on a standard 2cm to 400cm range.\n\n**Installation Instructions**\n\nPrior to mounting, ensure your microcontroller is capable of operating within a 3.3V to 5.0V DC power supply.\n\n1. Mount the proximity sensor to a suitable location, using M3 screw holes provided on the sensor's corners or a compatible substrate.\n2. Connect the sensor to your microcontroller using the 4-pin header, ensuring a secure connection to the VCC, GND, SDA, and SCL pins.\n3. Assign the I2C address of the sensor to the address 0x29 to facilitate communication.\n\n**Important Safety Information**\n\nHandling the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor requires proper ESD precautions to prevent damage. Exceeding a voltage of 5.5V or improper installation can result in permanent damage to the sensor.\n\nThis guide should provide a clear and straightforward installation process,",
