      "content": "I'll expand the draft to meet the complexity score requirements while maintaining clarity and usability.\n\n**Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Installation and Configuration Guide**\n\n**General Information**\n\n* Model Number: Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor\n* Voltage Range: 3.3V to 5.0V DC\n* Interface: I2C Protocol\n* Range: 2cm to 400cm\n\n**Electrical Specifications**\n\n* Power Supply: DC voltage within the specified range\n* Pinout:\n\t+ VCC: 5V when operating voltage exceeds 3.0V\n\t+ GND: 0V when operating voltage exceeds 3.3V\n\t+ SDA: IoT microcontroller's SDA pin\n\t+ SCL: IoT microcontroller's SCL pin\n\n**Installation Preparations**\n\nBefore mounting the proximity sensor, ensure that your microcontroller is compatible with the I2C protocol and can operate within the specified voltage range. Download and install any necessary firmware or drivers for I2C communication.\n\n**Mounting the Proximity Sensor**\n\n* Mount the proximity sensor to a suitable location on your device's chassis, using M3 screw holes provided on the sensor's corners or a compatible substrate.",
